# The history stores text with LF (verified: `git cat-file -p HEAD:README.md`
# comes back 242 bytes shorter than the working copy, which is one CR per line).
# `text=auto` is what keeps it that way: Git normalises to LF on commit and
# core.autocrlf hands this machine CRLF back on checkout, so nothing changes on
# disk and nothing churns in the history.
#
# An earlier version of this file said `-text` on the belief that the history
# was CRLF. It is not -- `git show` had applied the checkout conversion before
# the bytes were counted. `-text` would have started storing CRLF for every
# file committed from this machine, mixing endings into an LF history.
* text=auto
